<title>JORDAN: Libya donates 7,500 tonnes of durum wheat to Iraq.</title>
<headline>Libya donates 7,500 tonnes of durum wheat to Iraq.</headline>
<dateline>AMMAN 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Libya has donated 7,500 tonnes of bulk durum wheat to Iraq, Jordanian shipping sources said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>They said the vessel Madeira had left the Libyan port of Benghazi enroute to Iraq, but it was not immediately known whether it would offload in Jordan's Red Sea Aqaba port or Iraq's Umm Qasr in the Gulf, the sources said.</p>
<p>They said Libya had bought the wheat from Swiss supplier Andre.</p>
<p>Libya's news agency JANA reported last week that a ship loaded with foodstuffs was heading to sanctions-hit Iraq ahead of the holy month of Ramadan.</p>
<p>It did not give details but said the Iraqi envoy in Tripoli saw off the ship.</p>
<p>-- Amman Newsroom +9626-623776</p>
</text>
